{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q5264612","formula":"C₁₇H₁₇ClN₄","hill":"C17H17ClN4","elements":["H","C","N","Cl"],"composition":{"C":17.0,"H":17.0,"N":4.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Norclozapine"},"descriptions":{"en":"N-Desmethylclozapine (NDMC), or norclozapine, is a major active metabolite of the atypical antipsychotic drug clozapine. Unlike clozapine, it possesses intrinsic activity at the D2/D3 receptors, and acts as a weak partial agonist at these sites similarly to aripiprazole and bifeprunox. Notably, NDMC has also been shown to act as a potent and efficacious agonist at the muscarinic acetylcholine M1 receptor and the δ-opioid receptor, unlike clozapine as well."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":135409468,"mass":312.8,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1CN(CCN1)C2=NC3=C(C=CC(=C3)Cl)NC4=CC=CC=C42","inchikey":"JNNOSTQEZICQQP-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"3-chloro-6-piperazin-1-yl-11H-benzo[b][1,4]benzodiazepine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"135409468","atoms":39,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.734,"y":-0.396,"z":1.407,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.378,"y":-0.894,"z":0.865,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.841,"y":-0.038,"z":-0.225,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.629,"y":1.194,"z":-0.445,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.977,"y":1.864,"z":0.898,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.749,"y":1.014,"z":1.835,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.441,"y":0.022,"z":-0.358,"el":"C"},{"x":0.123,"y":1.195,"z":-0.3,"el":"N"},{"x":1.495,"y":1.463,"z":-0.369,"el":"C"},{"x":2.507,"y":0.68,"z":0.221,"el":"C"},{"x":3.83,"y":1.162,"z":0.231,"el":"C"},{"x":4.154,"y":2.387,"z":-0.352,"el":"C"},{"x":3.154,"y":3.147,"z":-0.945,"el":"C"},{"x":1.838,"y":2.695,"z":-0.946,"el":"C"},{"x":3.544,"y":4.661,"z":-1.662,"el":"Cl"},{"x":2.262,"y":-0.607,"z":0.76,"el":"N"},{"x":1.5,"y":-1.568,"z":0.062,"el":"C"},{"x":2.022,"y":-2.87,"z":-0.061,"el":"C"},{"x":1.371,"y":-3.845,